{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PRE-CLAIM FINDINGS — read-only investigation while this ticket is blocked. Recorded as information;\nthe description is NOT edited because eb6e is not claimable yet (0d76 blocks it).\n\n## 1. THE VOTER_ERROR ALARM ALREADY EXISTS — the Scope overstates the work\n\nThe Scope lists `infra/scripts/observability.sh — the VOTER_ERROR alarm` as a deliverable. It is\nalready built and shipped by story S4b (epic d251). The full chain is present:\n\n  src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py            `_voter_error()` writes a greppable VOTER_ERROR line to\n                                            stderr -> journald, and best-effort publishes the metric\n  infra/scripts/observability.sh  §4        greps the container journald, publishes\n                                            `rebar/host:voter_errors` as a per-interval delta\n  infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf         the `rebar-gerrit-voter-errors` alarm\n  infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md:110      \"Reading voter failures (VOTER_ERROR + the alarms)\"\n\nVERIFIED LIVE, not just present in source: `describe-alarms` in 896586841071/us-east-1 returns\n`StateValue: OK` with a FRESH datapoint, so the probe is actively publishing right now.\n\nCONSEQUENCE for the ORDERING criterion added to this ticket: its alarm half is largely a VERIFICATION\ntask, not a build task. The genuinely new deliverable is the `infra/runbooks/` KILL-SWITCH entry. An\nimplementer who takes the Scope at face value will try to build what exists and may DUPLICATE the\nmetric. The Scope should be corrected when this ticket is claimed.\n\n## 2. PROVING THE ALARM LIVE IS FEASIBLE FROM THIS ENVIRONMENT\n\nAccess confirmed: `aws sts` as arn:aws:iam::896586841071:user/joe_frontier, CloudWatch read, and SSM\nto the prod host i-00880b2c7f13527c5 (`PingStatus: Online`). Combined with the runbook's `/rerun`\nescape hatch and journald over SSM, there is a credible route to inducing a real VOTER_ERROR on the\nCURRENT Anthropic path and observing the alarm transition. So \"we cannot observe it from here\" is not\na valid reason to mark the ordering criterion met by inspection.\n\nDESIGN CAVEAT for whoever runs the drill: per bug c943 a 409 \"change is closed\" deliberately does NOT\nemit VOTER_ERROR, so using a closed change is the wrong way to induce one.\n\n## 3. THE S3 CONDITIONAL IN THE APPROACH IS RESOLVED — replace it with the fact\n\nThe Approach hedges: \"a cross-region inference profile as the throttling mitigation (subject to S3's\ncaching measurement -- if caching and inference profiles prove mutually exclusive ...)\". Ticket 2932\n(closed) settled it:\n\n  * ON-DEMAND MODEL IDS ARE NOT INVOKABLE AT ALL, so the on-demand-vs-profile comparison the hedge\n    contemplates is moot -- only inference profiles work.\n  * PROMPT CACHING WORKS WITH A REGIONAL INFERENCE PROFILE: `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` measured\n    cache_write=4017 on attempt 1 and cached on attempt 2.\n  * They are NOT mutually exclusive. `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` is the recorded verified caching\n    default.\nCorroborated by 2932's own comment \"PROMPT CACHING WORKS ON BEDROCK\" reporting cache_read=542,723 /\ncache_write=6,239 across 19 calls end-to-end.\n\nWhen this ticket is claimed, replace the conditional with the resolved fact so nobody re-runs the\nmeasurement.\n\n## Status\n\nNo plan review, no claim, no implementation, no commit, and THE MODEL FLIP WAS NOT PERFORMED --\n`REBAR_LLM_MODEL` untouched, `fetch-secrets.sh` untouched, the Anthropic key still fetched."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785726984259344001,"uuid":"133bb7fa-89c3-4fe6-be4d-e3d5c0791813"}